# Engineering Standards

These apply to every stack. Project-specific conventions live in
`.ai/conventions.md` and take precedence where they conflict.

## Code

- Match existing style, structure, and naming before introducing your own.
- Small functions, clear names, single responsibility. Delete dead code.
- No secrets, tokens, or credentials in source. Read config from env.
- Handle errors explicitly — never swallow them silently.

```txt
# BAD: silent failure hides bugs
try { doWork() } catch (e) {}

# GOOD: log with context and fail loudly / propagate
try { doWork() } catch (e) { logger.error("doWork failed", e); throw }
```

## Changes

- Keep diffs minimal and scoped to the task. No drive-by refactors mixed with features.
- Don't add comments that narrate the code. Comment only non-obvious *why*.
- Update or add tests alongside behavior changes (see `30-verification`).
- Update docs in `.ai/` when behavior, architecture, or conventions change.

## Dependencies

- Prefer the standard library and existing dependencies. Justify new ones in an ADR.
- Pin/lock versions via the project's package manager; never hand-invent versions.
